WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:33.030
<b>The First Kaisendon</b>

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.350
Yes!

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:51.160
<b>Kamil (24)
Eisenschmidt Employee</b>

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:51.160
<b>Ignaz (23)
Eisenschmidt Employee</b>

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.080
Our work at Eisenschmidt is finally over!

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:46.670
Starting tomorrow, we can make 
deals at our own discretion.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:47.700
Right.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.160
First step is to head north and 
get a stockpile of Jorsten wheat.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.930
Are we going to be okay, though?

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.180
It'll be our first deal and up 
north, and it's not very safe...

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.580
Hey, hey...

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.940
I thought you wanted to earn some 
last minute cash before the wedding?

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:09.020
N-Nobody has to overextend and put themselves 
in danger for my wedding though.

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:13.980
There's highwaymen and robbers, possibly 
poisonous insects or unknown diseases.

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:17.550
The water might not agree with us, and we might
not be able to sleep with a different pillow.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:21.100
And this is why they call 
you Kamil the Coward.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:24.200
You want to marry my little 
sister, do you not?!

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.570
O-Of course I do, Ignaz.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:30.010
Which is why I've gathered my 
courage to say this thing today.

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:31.040
Oh really?

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:34.080
I'd like to see just how brave you are.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:38.510
The palace guards told me 
about this restaurant.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:41.350
This restaurant will be 
a test of your courage.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.010
Welcome!

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.640
Welcome.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.150
It's so nice and warm in here.

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.150
And this warm towel feels 
so good on your hands.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:55.020
Two draft beers and a little 
stew as an appetizer.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.250
So this is the famous whatsontap.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:04.040
<b>Whatsontap Draft</b>

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:04.040
<b>Nothing better than this after a day at work</b>

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:01.370
This is ale... right?

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:02.700
Don't look so scared!

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.020
Let's hurry up and drink.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.270
Prosit!

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.040
<b>Fizz</b>

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:20.290
Delicious!

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:22.950
Excuse me, another whatsontap please!

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:23.700
Coming up!

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.790
Would you also like another?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:29.780
This was good, but I'd like 
something stronger next.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:32.060
How about some reishu then?

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.470
Rei... shu?

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:36.080
Yeah, I'll have that.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.800
<b>Chikuzenni</b>

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.800
<b>Stew with a rich dashi flavor!
 Great as a side-dish, or with drinks.</b>

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.800
So these are some cooked vegetables, huh?

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.140
This is good, too!

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.170
You're right!

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.880
Thank you for waiting.

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:57.200
Another draft beer, and your reishu.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.720
<b>Reishu</b>

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:57.720
<b>Fragrant Japanese rice wine, enjoy it cold</b>

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:01.680
Wow. This looks so clear, like water.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:07.100
<b>Crisp</b>

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.460
Whoa, it's so crisp yet so tasty!

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.500
It's my first time trying 
sake, but I like it.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.650
<i>Appetizers and whatsontap.</i>

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:18.650
<i>Appetizers and reishu.</i>

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:20.910
<i>It's a perfect pairing!</i>

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:23.590
Why'd you have to scare me like that, Ignaz?

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.220
This is a great place.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.510
I'm ready for this kind of trial any day!

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:33.650
Your real trial is still ahead, Kamil.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:38.470
Have you decided what you'd like to order?

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.120
I'd like to order some fish.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.530
Don't scare me.

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:44.430
And keep it raw!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.830
Now just a minute!

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:47.840
Raw fish?!

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.800
You've got to be joking, Ignaz!

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.760
This may be an unusual restaurant, but 
you still don't serve fish raw. Right?!

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.330
The sashimi, then? It's a point 
of pride at our establishment.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.990
You do serve it? R-R-Raw fish?

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:05.030
No, no, no, I may be able to 
prove my courage with this,

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.770
but are you serious?

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:07.990
If things go wrong, I could die!

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:08.950
Maybe.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.470
"Never eat raw fish" is a 
saying that has been passed

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:15.200
down from my great-great-great-grandfather!

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.200
Relax.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:17.460
The dish is certified tasty!

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.570
I'm less concerned about the taste 
and more concerned about my <i>life</i>!

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.920
I'll take the wurst.

00:04:22.920 --> 00:04:25.320
Coming right up.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:28.590
You're not having the raw fish?

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.340
Of course not!

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:34.360
If both of us collapse, who 
will go buy the Jorsten wheat?

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:39.100
You're okay with your sister 
becoming a widow already?

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.600
Don't talk like that, Kamil.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.500
If you finish that raw fish, 
you can make me do one thing.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:46.830
Anything you want.

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:53.770
But if you don't finish it, I'll have to 
reconsider your marriage to my little sister.

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:54.840
All right.

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.100
Then it's settled!

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:59.450
<i>Forgive me, Kamil.</i>

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:02.090
<i>This is part of being an older brother.</i>

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:05.100
<i>I will see if you're brave enough.</i>

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:06.810
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:07.940
Here it is!

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.140
Yellowtail sashimi.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.580
I recommend eating it with soy sauce.

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:13.730
What?

00:05:13.730 --> 00:05:15.870
Th-This is raw fish?

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:29.110
<b>Yellowtail Sashimi</b>

00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:29.110
<b>Amply marbled yellowtail. Tasty even 
without growing up to be an amberjack.</b>

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:18.520
This shine, this color.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.970
It looks like fruit more than anything.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:22.800
Beautiful.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.250
No.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:25.930
I can't let myself be 
fooled by this exterior.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:28.110
This is <i>raw fish</i>!

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:33.570
<i>Kamil is showing his true courage!</i>

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:36.080
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.050
<i>I knew what a wonderful man you are.</i>

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.680
<i>You're too cautious and think too much,</i>

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:47.390
<i>to the point that it's seen as cowardice.</i>

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:50.850
<i>Hey, that's enough!</i>

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.860
<i>That's raw fish, you know!</i>

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:56.290
<i>O-Oh, no!</i>

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:58.660
<i>I was planning on stopping him!</i>

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.980
<i>If Kamil gets food poisoning from this,</i>

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.230
<i>or should the worst-case scenario happen...</i>

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:09.140
<i>What am I going to tell my sister?</i>

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.230
A-Are you okay?

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:29.020
H-Hey... don't tell me that's... 
is that actually... g-good?

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.200
<i>No, no, no, no.</i>

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:38.710
<b>Growl</b>

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.660
E-Excuse me. I'm sorry, but 
could I get some sashimi, too?

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:46.160
Coming right up!

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.810
You know, if you're hungry though, 
I would recommend our kaisendon.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.260
Kaisendon?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:56.410
Yes! It's seafood sashimi 
on rice, served in a bowl.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:58.110
All right.

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.860
Then I'll have one of your kaisendon.

00:07:00.860 --> 00:07:03.140
So that's one kaisendon.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:04.510
Coming right up.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:06.300
<i>Just you wait, Kamil.</i>

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:09.960
<i>If you ate it, I have no 
choice but to eat it, too.</i>

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.510
<i>Otherwise, how could I look 
my sister in the face?</i>

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.050
<i>That's it!</i>

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:16.520
<i>Sometimes, a man's gotta 
do what a man's gotta do.</i>

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:17.780
Thank you for your patience.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:19.990
Nobu's special kaisendon.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:26.360
<b>Nobu's Special 
Kaisendon</b>

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:26.360
<b>A rice bowl generously topped with
fruits of the sea. Best enjoyed
with wasabi and soy sauce.</b>

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:26.350
S-So this is the kaisendon?

00:07:26.350 --> 00:07:28.680
This red meat here is tuna.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:33.980
Then we have salmon, yellowtail, 
beakfish, squid, sweet shrimp...

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:37.200
A-And these jewel-like things are...

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:38.460
It's ikura.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:42.090
They're salmon roe and very delicious.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:46.260
Mix the wasabi and soy sauce 
on this little plate and

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:49.070
then pour it over the bowl.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:58.980
<i>This is rice?</i>

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:01.560
<i>When she said 'gohan' she 
was talking about rice.</i>

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:05.630
<i>I'll join you in your world now, Kamil.</i>

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.310
<b>Wave crashing</b>

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:18.640
<i>It's the sea!</i>

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:31.660
<b>Rich rich rich</b>

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:21.400
<i>What is this savory flavor?!</i>

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.030
<i>That's it.</i>

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:24.720
<i>It's the rich flavor of the 
yellowtail melting in my mouth,</i>

00:08:24.720 --> 00:08:26.650
<i>accented with the wasabi and soy sauce.</i>

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:31.670
<i>And then there's the rice, gently taking 
it all in and tying it all together.</i>

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.200
<i>Next up is this tuna thing.</i>

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:42.430
<b>Bold~</b>

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.930
<i>This bold taste reminds me of meat.</i>

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.440
<i>And the flavor is so complex.</i>

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:43.880
<i>Next up, the squid.</i>

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:46.140
<i>Ooh, the squid is good, too.</i>

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:48.670
<i>A unique texture paired with sweetness.</i>

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:53.690
<i>All these competing savory 
flavors of the sashimi.</i>

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:57.950
<i>This is truly a dance performance that 
the fish are performing in this bowl!</i>

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:00.460
<i>Kaisendon is amazing!</i>

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:04.100
Here you go.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:14.260
<i>The reishu is cleansing the 
sashimi's ocean flavor away.</i>

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:16.590
<i>Kaisendon.</i>

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:17.460
<i>Reishu.</i>

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:18.970
<i>Kaisendon.</i>

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:19.830
<i>Reishu.</i>

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.340
They're perfect together!

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.600
That was so good.

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:30.760
I want to swim in this 
sea of flavor forever.

00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:32.000
Ignaz.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.350
Ignaz!

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.500
This kaisendon is great, huh?

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:42.490
All right. Now for your promise.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:44.150
Oh, yeah.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:46.810
I promised I would do one 
thing you asked of me.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.360
Just don't make it too out there.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:52.180
I never could bring myself to say it.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:56.640
But today, you gave this old coward a push.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:09:58.520
Kamil.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:01.820
Brother.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:04.170
I'd like to call you 
that, if it's all right.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.630
Two whatsontaps, please!

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:12.820
This guy is going to be 
marrying my little sister!

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.460
Congratulations!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.570
Congratulations.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:17.580
Thank you, everyone.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.940
Thank you, Brother.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:27.470
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:23.990
All right, let's toast!

00:10:24.600 --> 00:10:25.870
Prosit!

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.280
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:38.700
<b>Tawaramachi</b>

00:10:35.590 --> 00:10:38.710
We've come here to Tawaramachi.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:41.850
Japan's oldest subway passes through here.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.850
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:46.000
This area has changed quite a bit, 
but let's have a look, shall we?

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:47.150
Let's do that.

00:10:46.490 --> 00:10:51.010
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.730
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:53.160
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu".

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:53.460
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:56.520
Kaisendon, huh? It's so good.

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:58.110
I love it, too!

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:02.750
That is a dish where I sort of think, 
"Man, I'm so glad that I was born Japanese."

00:11:02.750 --> 00:11:03.770
So true.

00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:06.160
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi.</b>

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:07.040
This is it, Enshuuya.

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:10.420
<b>Asakusa Fish Cuisine Enshuuya</b>

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:09.930
Right, this place is famous 
for their kaisendon.

00:11:09.930 --> 00:11:10.710
Shall we go in?

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:11.590
Let's!

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:16.280
So you have that fish tank there. 
Does that mean that you're

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:18.330
focusing on seafood cuisine?

00:11:18.090 --> 00:11:21.390
<b>Asakusa Fish Cuisine Enshuuya
 2nd Generation Chef: Angui Nobuaki</b>

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:20.130
Yes, Enshuuya does a fish cuisine.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:21.390
Ah, fish.

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:24.430
Ah, it does say fish cuisine here.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.190
That's not something that's said lightly.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:27.440
Well, I suppose if you could just write it.

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:28.730
You're right.

00:11:28.270 --> 00:11:28.990
Oh, you!

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:32.500
So earlier, I saw something 
tasty in this anime.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:35.910
So they have a lot of 
different dishes here. Oh?!

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:38.020
Here you go.

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:38.510
Oh, this is marvelous.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.440
This is impressive!

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:46.040
The dish that's almost 
a must before kaisendon!

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.030
This broiled fish head is really good.

00:11:51.620 --> 00:11:59.120
This sweet, spicy broiled flavor, it reminds 
me of my mom's cooking when I was small.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:03.830
When it comes to broiling, 
you know, you need some skills.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:05.090
Exactly.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:09.250
This flavor is not something that 
you can whip up out of nowhere.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:11.060
Really well said!

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:15.480
Yeah, this is great.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:19.040
The chef has started cutting the sashimi.

00:12:20.710 --> 00:12:21.980
This means it's almost time!

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:26.020
This is it, right? I came 
here for this kaisendon.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:32.620
I did get distracted by all sorts 
of other things, but this is it.

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:38.080
You know at sushi places? There are 
people who order nigiri as a snack?

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:41.130
That's not the thing that'll fill you up.

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:44.050
This here is called "atama" 
(head), the stuff that's on top.

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:47.010
<b>The topping is called "atama" (head)</b>

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:48.320
So you can just go for the 
"atama" and eat it like this.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.650
And then you do this.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:53.530
Aha!

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:58.810
You do about half with just the "atama," 
and then you eat the rest normally

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:02.860
to finish it up. That's 
apparently a good way to do it.

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:04.990
That's a professional for you.

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:08.250
The sashimi, the sake, and 
the rice all taste great.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:09.260
Oh?

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.500
It would be great if there was someone 
who would pour sake like this.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.230
I'm a bit past my prime, but how about it?

00:13:13.230 --> 00:13:14.570
Well, I'm not that desperate.

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:15.810
Fine, just pour it yourself then!

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:22.070
I'm happy.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:23.090
Satisfaction!

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:26.830
Even Nagira-san was convinced by 
"Asakusa Fish Cuisine Enshuuya."

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:29.100
It's about one minute 
from Tawaramachi Station.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:29.060
<b>Assistance: Gurunabi                                 To be continued</b>

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:32.380
If you want to have a good 
kaisendon, then come here. Here!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:57.980
<b>Next Time...
Shinobu-chan's Special Napolitan</b>

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:54.540
Next time on "Isekai Izakaya"
aka "Izakaya Nobu in Aitheria."

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:57.510
Please sample the tasty tales.
